<!-- The N.D. Iowa memorandum's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of the
     typst template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 12 pt (size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst
     pitch, LR 10(b)(1) double spaced) with a half-inch indent, and the headings in them; the caption, contents,
     quotation, service-list, signature and footer lines in 13.8 pt boxes (typst pitch-single); letter page with 1-inch
     margins (LR 10(b)(3)) and a centered page number (LR 10(b)), its line 36.6 pt above the page foot (732 twips:
     where typst sets it, footer-descent 30 %). docx/motion-brief.lua writes every paragraph's own spacing. Twips:
     20 x pt. pandoc reads without smart punctuation: the filter sets quotes, dashes and ellipses as the typst
     template's markdown reader (cmarker) does, quote by quote. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" pandoc-from="markdown-smart" base="xengine" size="24" body="480" single="276" indent="720" heading="480" heading-before="0" heading-after="0" footer="732"/>
